tls_mbedtls: register the client certificate only when one was loaded

tls_open() always calls mbedtls_ssl_conf_own_cert(), also when no
cert_file/cert_pem was given, so mbedTLS gets an empty certificate and an
empty key. When a server asks for an optional client certificate (Caddy
client_auth mode verify_if_given, nginx ssl_verify_client optional),
mbedTLS answers with that empty certificate and then fails to sign the
CertificateVerify with the empty key: "TLS handshake failed." on TLS 1.3,
"mbedtls_ssl_handshake returned -0x3e80" on TLS 1.2. Without an own
certificate configured, mbedTLS sends an empty certificate list instead,
which a server with an optional request accepts. A configured certificate
(cert_file/key_file, mpv's tls-cert-file/tls-key-file) and the generated
one of a listening socket are still registered as before.

Issue: https://github.com/midasvo/libmpv-android/issues/56
       (https://github.com/midasvo/ephyra/issues/960)
Upstream: the same code is in FFmpeg n7.1.1, n8.1, n9.0.2, n9.1 and master
(checked 2026-11-24); not sent yet, worth sending to FFmpeg. Drop this
patch once an FFmpeg release contains a fix.

diff --git a/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c b/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
index 211652d..c514069 100644
--- a/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
+++ b/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
@@ -646,8 +646,11 @@ static int tls_open(URLContext *h, const char *uri, int flags, AVDictionary **op
     mbedtls_ssl_conf_rng(&tls_ctx->ssl_config, mbedtls_ctr_drbg_random, &tls_ctx->ctr_drbg_context);
     mbedtls_ssl_conf_ca_chain(&tls_ctx->ssl_config, &tls_ctx->ca_cert, NULL);
 
-    // set own certificate and private key
-    if ((ret = mbedtls_ssl_conf_own_cert(&tls_ctx->ssl_config, &tls_ctx->own_cert, &tls_ctx->priv_key)) != 0) {
+    // set own certificate and private key, only when one was loaded: an empty one
+    // is sent when a server asks for an optional client certificate, and then the
+    // handshake fails because nothing can sign with the empty key
+    if (tls_ctx->own_cert.raw.p &&
+        (ret = mbedtls_ssl_conf_own_cert(&tls_ctx->ssl_config, &tls_ctx->own_cert, &tls_ctx->priv_key)) != 0) {
         av_log(h, AV_LOG_ERROR, "mbedtls_ssl_conf_own_cert returned %d\n", ret);
         goto fail;
     }
